The GPL licence option is selected for this kext. Original notices remain in
every compiled source. No firmware is included.

pd_cd321x_events.h follows cd321x_interrupt's exact EVENT1/CLEAR1 64-bit
acknowledgement ordering from the same pinned source. It does not change an
interrupt mask or enable GPIO/AIC interrupts. Native sampling remains 1 Hz.

pd_cd321x_mask.h follows tipd_init and tipd_cd321x_data's startup MASK1:
plug/power-status/data-status events (bits1/9/10), with checked readback.
It is CD3217/T8103-specific and does not enable a GPIO/AIC interrupt.

pd_cd321x_control.h uses the read-only event1/mask1/S0/status/data register
layout from the same pinned Linux tipd/core.c, retaining Intel/Heikki Krogerus
and Asahi notices, GPL-2.0. It acknowledges no interrupts and changes no mask.
The native command-gate adapter and host failure tests use that actual helper.
